{% raw %}{% endraw %}{{ human_friendly_app_name | upper }}{% raw %} - INSTALLATION GUIDE
===============================

{% endraw %}{{ product_id }}{% raw %}-<version>.msi installs {% endraw %}{{ human_friendly_app_name }}{% raw %} as a Windows service.


WHAT IT INSTALLS
----------------

- The {% endraw %}{{ human_friendly_app_name }}{% raw %} application under:
      C:\Program Files\{% endraw %}{{ company_id }}{% raw %}\{% endraw %}{{ product_id }}{% raw %}\
- A Windows service named "{% endraw %}{{ service_name }}{% raw %}" that serves the app at:
      http://127.0.0.1:{% endraw %}{{ backend_deployed_port_number }}{% raw %}
- A log directory (kept on upgrade and uninstall) under:
      C:\ProgramData\{% endraw %}{{ company_id }}{% raw %}\{% endraw %}{{ product_id }}{% raw %}\logs\


REQUIREMENTS
------------

- Windows 10/11 or Windows Server, 64-bit.
- Administrator rights to install (it registers a system service).


INTERACTIVE INSTALL
-------------------

1. Double-click {% endraw %}{{ product_id }}{% raw %}-<version>.msi and accept the elevation prompt.

2. Accept the license and confirm the install location.

3. On the "Service account" page, choose how the service runs:

   - LocalSystem (default, recommended).

   - A specific low-privilege account. Enter the user as .\name (local) or
     DOMAIN\name, plus the password. The installer grants that account the
     "Log on as a service" right.

4. Finish the install. Leave "Open {% endraw %}{{ human_friendly_app_name }}{% raw %}" checked to open
   http://127.0.0.1:{% endraw %}{{ backend_deployed_port_number }}{% raw %}/ in your browser.


SILENT / UNATTENDED INSTALL
---------------------------

   msiexec /i {% endraw %}{{ product_id }}{% raw %}-<version>.msi /qn

/qn = no UI; /qb = progress bar only. Silent installs never open a browser.

Set any of these properties on the command line:

   SERVICE_ACCOUNT    Default LocalSystem. Use "custom" to run as a supplied
                      account.
   SERVICE_USER       Account name when SERVICE_ACCOUNT=custom, e.g. .\svcaccount
   SERVICE_PASSWORD   Password for that account.
   PORT               Default {% endraw %}{{ backend_deployed_port_number }}{% raw %}. TCP port the service listens on.

Examples:

   LocalSystem, default port:
      msiexec /i {% endraw %}{{ product_id }}{% raw %}-1.2.3.msi /qn

   Dedicated low-privilege account:
      msiexec /i {% endraw %}{{ product_id }}{% raw %}-1.2.3.msi /qn SERVICE_ACCOUNT=custom SERVICE_USER=.\svcaccount SERVICE_PASSWORD=YourPassword

   Capture a log of the install for troubleshooting:
      msiexec /i {% endraw %}{{ product_id }}{% raw %}-1.2.3.msi /qn /l*v install.log


AFTER INSTALL
-------------

- Service status:  Get-Service {% endraw %}{{ service_name }}{% raw %}   (should be Running)
- App:             http://127.0.0.1:{% endraw %}{{ backend_deployed_port_number }}{% raw %}/
- Logs:            C:\ProgramData\{% endraw %}{{ company_id }}{% raw %}\{% endraw %}{{ product_id }}{% raw %}\logs\


UPGRADE
-------

Run a newer {% endraw %}{{ product_id }}{% raw %}-<version>.msi. It replaces the installed version in
place and keeps the data under C:\ProgramData\{% endraw %}{{ company_id }}{% raw %}\{% endraw %}{{ product_id }}{% raw %}\.


UNINSTALL
---------

Settings > Apps (or Control Panel > Programs) > {% endraw %}{{ human_friendly_app_name }}{% raw %} > Uninstall, or:

   msiexec /x {% endraw %}{{ product_id }}{% raw %}-<version>.msi /qn

This stops and removes the service and the program files. The data directory
(C:\ProgramData\{% endraw %}{{ company_id }}{% raw %}\{% endraw %}{{ product_id }}{% raw %}\) is left in place.


TROUBLESHOOTING
---------------

- Service will not start: check C:\ProgramData\{% endraw %}{{ company_id }}{% raw %}\{% endraw %}{{ product_id }}{% raw %}\logs\ and
  the Windows Event Log (Application).

- Custom account install fails to start the service: confirm the account
  name/password and that it was granted "Log on as a service".

- Port {% endraw %}{{ backend_deployed_port_number }}{% raw %} already in use: reinstall with a different PORT.
